$\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ |" 13194139534299 17592186045417 true] [17592186418084 1072 #uuid "098ae999-41d1-5d21-93d9-672720b112c8" 13194139534299 17592186045417 true] [17592186418084 1074 "We can compute the variance of a discrete random variable $X$ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $\\text{E}[X].$ Summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3)+4\\cdot f(4)+5\\cdot f(5)+6\\cdot f(6) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{8})+2(\\frac{3}{8})+3(\\frac{1}{4})+4(\\frac{1}{8})+5(\\frac{1}{16})+6(\\frac{1}{16}) \\\\  & =\\frac{45}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$ Summing up the products of each value of ${X}^{2}$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={1}^{2}\\cdot f(1)+{2}^{2}\\cdot f(2)+{3}^{2}\\cdot f(3)+{4}^{2}\\cdot f(4)+{5}^{2}\\cdot f(5)+{6}^{2}\\cdot f(6) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{8})+4(\\frac{3}{8})+9(\\frac{1}{4})+16(\\frac{1}{8})+25(\\frac{1}{16})+36(\\frac{1}{16}) \\\\  & =\\frac{155}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{155}{16}-{(\\frac{45}{16})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{155}{16}-\\frac{2025}{256} \\\\  & =\\frac{455}{256}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534299 17592186045417 true] [17592186418085 1068 #edb/ref 17592186418082 13194139534299 17592186045417 true] [17592186418085 1069 "q-129104" 13194139534299 17592186045417 true] [17592186418085 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534299 17592186045417 true] [17592186418085 1071 "Two fair  four-sided dice are rolled and $X$ is the absolute difference of their scores. The probability mass function $f(x)$ of $X$ is shown in the table below. What is $\\text{Var}[X]?$ \n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{2}{8}$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ | $\\frac{2}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |" 13194139534299 17592186045417 true] [17592186418085 1072 #uuid "b04f202f-7340-5122-b2d5-59ca0d357302" 13194139534299 17592186045417 true] [17592186418085 1074 "The variance of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}(x-\\text{E}[X])^{2}\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $\\text{E}[X].$ Summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =0\\cdot f(0)+1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3) \\\\  & =0(\\frac{2}{8})+1(\\frac{3}{8})+2(\\frac{2}{8})+3(\\frac{1}{8}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{5}{4}$ into the variance formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}{(x-\\frac{5}{4})}^{2}\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the variance as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & ={(0-\\frac{5}{4})}^{2}\\cdot f(0)+{(1-\\frac{5}{4})}^{2}\\cdot f(1)+{(2-\\frac{5}{4})}^{2}\\cdot f(2)+{(3-\\frac{5}{4})}^{2}\\cdot f(3) \\\\  & ={(-\\frac{5}{4})}^{2}\\cdot f(0)+{(-\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}\\cdot f(1)+{(\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}\\cdot f(2)+{(\\frac{7}{4})}^{2}\\cdot f(3) \\\\  & =(\\frac{25}{16})(\\frac{2}{8})+(\\frac{1}{16})(\\frac{3}{8})+(\\frac{9}{16})(\\frac{2}{8})+(\\frac{49}{16})(\\frac{1}{8}) \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{16}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534299 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-26cb8fc2-022b-568c-b41a-7bbf10255e99" 17592186418072 "answer-5782b94b-8258-5e43-85df-a8d0c1327515" 17592186418073 "answer-585f608f-5a28-539a-9ae1-19a60685c3c2" 17592186418074 "answer-637b3062-8acc-5b54-9040-15b955fa09f3" 17592186418075 "answer-96670029-c0b7-54da-8a19-99c6872c02f4" 17592186418076 "answer-d098068f-0f1e-5a9a-b34b-77d4043a3eac" 17592186418077 "answer-dc6e32fe-4a49-5537-a523-6b3d99454374" 17592186418078 "answer-f3700714-cf33-5fb7-9887-c4e1c1ca2d27" 17592186418079 "answer-f963b964-0ba8-5f1